FAQ

Q: What is a Display Driver IC?

A: A Display Driver IC is a semiconductor component that controls electrical signals sent to display pixels to produce images and visual content.

Q: Where are Display Driver ICs used?

A: DDICs are used in smartphones, televisions, monitors, tablets, automotive displays, wearable devices and other electronic products.

Q: What drives Display Driver IC demand?

A: Growth in smart devices, advanced OLED and LCD displays, higher resolutions and automotive display applications supports DDIC demand.

